  "term": "factor theory of personality",
  "definition": "Factor theory of personality is an approach that describes personality in terms of five main dimensions. In this source, those dimensions are extroversion, orderliness, emotional stability, accommodation, and intellectual curiosity, considered in terms of how much each is present or absent.",
